WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.967
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:09.002
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.302 --> 00:00:14.752
Unit seven: Identity & Fashion. Today you will use the passive voice with modals.

4
00:00:15.052 --> 00:00:17.635
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.135
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.983 --> 00:00:24.565
Self-representation.

7
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:29.152
Self-representation means how you show yourself to others.

8
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.226
Clothes are a form of self-representation.

9
00:00:32.817 --> 00:00:36.224
Your turn. Say: Self-representation.

10
00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:40.753
Self-representation.

11
00:00:41.517 --> 00:00:42.924
Cultural attire.

12
00:00:43.917 --> 00:00:47.054
Cultural attire means the traditional clothes of a culture.

13
00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:49.777
We wear cultural attire at weddings.

14
00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:53.488
Your turn. Say: Cultural attire.

15
00:00:56.333 --> 00:00:57.590
Cultural attire.

16
00:00:58.350 --> 00:00:59.699
Gender expression.

17
00:01:00.683 --> 00:01:04.459
Gender expression means how a person shows their gender through style.

18
00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:08.501
Gender expression can include clothes, hair and style.

19
00:01:09.117 --> 00:01:11.897
Your turn. Say: Gender expression.

20
00:01:14.733 --> 00:01:16.176
Gender expression.

21
00:01:16.917 --> 00:01:17.732
Norm.

22
00:01:18.717 --> 00:01:22.086
Norm means what is usual or expected in a society.

23
00:01:22.683 --> 00:01:24.973
Wearing a uniform is the norm at school.

24
00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:27.992
Your turn. Say: Norm.

25
00:01:30.833 --> 00:01:31.683
Norm.

26
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:33.834
Nonconformity.

27
00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:38.545
Nonconformity means not following the usual rules or styles.

28
00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:41.382
His bright hair shows nonconformity.

29
00:01:41.983 --> 00:01:44.740
Your turn. Say: Nonconformity.

30
00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.100
Nonconformity.

31
00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:51.025
Personal statement.

32
00:01:52.017 --> 00:01:55.038
Personal statement means something that shows who you are.

33
00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.859
My sneakers are a personal statement.

34
00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:01.474
Your turn. Say: Personal statement.

35
00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:05.671
Personal statement.

36
00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:07.650
Symbolic meaning.

37
00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:11.752
Symbolic meaning means an idea that a thing represents.

38
00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:15.220
The krama has a symbolic meaning for Khmer people.

39
00:02:15.817 --> 00:02:18.434
Your turn. Say: Symbolic meaning.

40
00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.522
Symbolic meaning.

41
00:02:23.283 --> 00:02:24.795
Social perception.

42
00:02:25.783 --> 00:02:29.246
Social perception means how society sees someone.

43
00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.082
Clothes can change social perception.

44
00:02:32.683 --> 00:02:35.707
Your turn. Say: Social perception.

45
00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:40.067
Social perception.

46
00:02:40.817 --> 00:02:41.969
Confidence.

47
00:02:42.983 --> 00:02:45.250
Confidence means believing in yourself.

48
00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.954
The right outfit gives me confidence.

49
00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:51.423
Your turn. Say: Confidence.

50
00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:55.500
Confidence.

51
00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:57.518
Inclusivity.

52
00:02:58.517 --> 00:03:01.712
Inclusivity means making everyone feel welcome.

53
00:03:02.317 --> 00:03:04.885
The fashion show celebrated inclusivity.

54
00:03:05.483 --> 00:03:08.194
Your turn. Say: Inclusivity.

55
00:03:11.033 --> 00:03:12.371
Inclusivity.

56
00:03:13.117 --> 00:03:14.083
Diversity.

57
00:03:15.083 --> 00:03:17.640
Diversity means many different kinds of people.

58
00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.226
Our class has great diversity.

59
00:03:20.817 --> 00:03:23.457
Your turn. Say: Diversity.

60
00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.243
Diversity.

61
00:03:27.983 --> 00:03:29.182
Acceptance.

62
00:03:30.183 --> 00:03:33.437
Acceptance means agreeing that people are fine as they are.

63
00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.456
Acceptance makes people feel safe.

64
00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.876
Your turn. Say: Acceptance.

65
00:03:42.733 --> 00:03:43.862
Acceptance.

66
00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:48.434
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:49.283 --> 00:03:52.432
Visal, how does fashion reflect identity in your culture?

68
00:03:53.517 --> 00:03:58.430
Cultural attire can be worn to show pride, like the sampot at weddings.

69
00:03:59.517 --> 00:04:00.657
And the krama?

70
00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:08.164
It has a symbolic meaning. It can be used as a scarf, a hat or a bag!

71
00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:11.133
What about young people's style?

72
00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:17.282
Fashion can be used for self-expression. I think diversity should be accepted.

73
00:04:18.433 --> 00:04:20.201
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:23.978
Grammar focus: Passive voice with modals.

75
00:04:24.278 --> 00:04:25.512
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:26.217 --> 00:04:28.611
Fashion can be used for self-expression.

77
00:04:29.517 --> 00:04:31.539
Diversity should be accepted.

78
00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:34.496
Uniforms must be worn at school.

79
00:04:35.433 --> 00:04:39.723
After a modal, use 'be' + past participle. Never 'is' or 'are'.

80
00:04:40.483 --> 00:04:43.867
Be careful! Don't say: Diversity should is accepted.

81
00:04:45.833 --> 00:04:48.518
Say: Diversity should be accepted.

82
00:04:48.818 --> 00:04:51.700
After a modal, use 'be' + past participle.

83
00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.152
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:55.967 --> 00:04:57.304
What We Wear.

85
00:04:57.604 --> 00:05:00.428
Fashion can be a form of self-representation.

86
00:05:01.433 --> 00:05:04.501
Cultural attire, like the sampot, is worn with pride.

87
00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.533
The krama has a symbolic meaning for many Cambodians.

88
00:05:09.533 --> 00:05:13.495
Embracing diversity and inclusivity allows greater acceptance.

89
00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.720
Everyone's style should be respected.

90
00:05:17.833 --> 00:05:21.974
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:22.817 --> 00:05:24.944
Diversity should blank accepted.

92
00:05:25.244 --> 00:05:28.270
A, be. B, is. C, being.

93
00:05:31.833 --> 00:05:33.357
The answer is A: be.

94
00:05:34.517 --> 00:05:37.410
The traditional clothes of a culture are cultural blank.

95
00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:41.340
A, attire. B, norms. C, statements.

96
00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.807
The answer is A: attire.

97
00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.309
Making everyone feel welcome is blank.

98
00:05:50.609 --> 00:05:54.936
A, inclusivity. B, nonconformity. C, perception.

99
00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.068
The answer is A: inclusivity.

100
00:06:02.267 --> 00:06:05.708
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:09.641
How does fashion reflect identity in your culture?

102
00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:20.008
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:20.308 --> 00:06:31.018
In Cambodia, traditional clothes are worn at weddings and festivals. Fashion can also be used to show your personality, and every style should be respected.

104
00:06:31.318 --> 00:06:33.097
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:33.983 --> 00:06:38.435
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and passive voice with modals.

106
00:06:38.735 --> 00:06:44.116
Today's value is respect for differences. Everyone is different, and everyone is special.

107
00:06:44.416 --> 00:06:46.894
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

108
00:06:47.194 --> 00:06:50.171
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

